aving access  we have 20 000 sites that you can get a  free pcr test and even right now as we  speak we're scaling up rapid  pcr testing federally federal sites for  pcr testing  in places that have the highest demand  including new york  dr wolinski with all of these people  testing positive these days and more  positives expected in january people are  looking at that 10-day isolation period  that's still in effect even if you're  vaccinated and boosted meanwhile the uk  has reduced it to seven days delta co  wants a reduction here we've heard one  of our frequent guests dr ashish jah say  to friends he recommends as little as  five days could we see movement from the  cdc on that quarantine period  yeah it's a great question we're  actively examining those data now and  i'm doing some modeling analyses to  assess that and we anticipate that we'll  have some updates soon  dr wolinski more than a thousand  children have died of covert in the u.s  they currently make up a quarter of the  cases 90 of children aren't vaccinated  so a lot of parents like myself are  trying to figure out how to navigate not  just through the holidays but also with  school so what do you think we should do  should we gather with our friends and  family and do you believe schools should  be shut down  right so several things in there nate  first the best way we can protect our  children is to get them vaccinated  children above the age of five are all  eligible for vaccination and we are  really working to get our children  vaccinated to protect them from disease  if your child is less than five the best  way to protect them is to surround them  with people who are vaccinated  themselves who are boosted themselves in  terms of the holiday how do we do the  holidays safely certainly you want to  make sure that you're vaccinated and  boosted if you're eligible and that the  people who you're gathering with are  vaccinated and eligible as well but i  want to highlight one important piece  an